                <pb facs="1124" n="1000" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg1000"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119E/12: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Mission at Lausanne to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract—Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lausanne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-05-04T11:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1923—11
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 5—6:14 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>290. Mission’s 278 of May 2 and 286 of May 4. Rumbold with good grace has
                    abandoned his opposition to participation in the work of the subcommittee by
                    members of our Mission. Tonight<anchor n="9" xml:id="d847-f1"/> he sent his
                    legal expert to ask who would represent us in the meeting of legal experts
                    tomorrow. Tentatively, I named Turlington. Now we shall be represented on all
                    subcommittees dealing with matters in which we have an interest.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d847-f1" n="9" xml:id="d847-f1-content">
                <p>Apparently this telegram was drafted on the night of May 3.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
